+### Same-operation failed source restart
+
+`Transaction::restart_failed_asset(writer)` consumes only its own unpublished writer for one declared logical asset under the existing original operation and writer exclusion. It positively seals the existing partial/3 record, closes that writer, and reopens the exact operation, partial proof and staged object. Original stage identity, ServiceLease identity, operation/configuration revision, asset declaration, native object identity, actual length and complete partial hash must still match. Only those authenticated unfinished bytes and their proof may be unlinked through the existing platform custody path; a fresh CreateNew writer begins at zero. Final cached files, all other assets, older stage generations and receipts are preserved. Foreign/replaced/linked/unsealed bytes refuse without adoption or truncation. Failure cannot claim Ready, deletion or successful restart.
+
+This is local transaction custody only: it grants no network, retry, deadline, scope, consent or configuration authority. Service admits a backup only within its original bounded source attempt/per-part deadline/cancellation contract and retains sanitized failed-source diagnostics. A failed seal or local custody check stops, and the original file/evidence remains for explicit recovery. The internal sealed-writer bit is not persisted and does not pretend that a partial asset was published. Existing assets/3 and partial/3 serialized bytes are unchanged.
